* own model: Texas Instruments SN74AXC4T774 (ring U10), 4-bit dual-supply level shifter with a direction pin per bit, built only from the maker's datasheet SCES898C (design/datasheets/w1_ti_sn74axc4t774.pdf, PDF pages). No SPICE model of this part is public on the maker's site (see models/SOURCES.md).
* ports: a1 a2 a3 a4 b1 b2 b3 b4 vcca vccb dir1 dir2 dir3 dir4 oe
* input thresholds (p5 Table 5.3): VCCI 1.1 to 1.95 V: VIH 0.65 VCCI, VIL 0.35 VCCI; 2.3 to 2.7 V: 1.6 V, 0.7 V; 3 to 3.6 V: 2.0 V, 0.8 V; 0.65 to 1 V: 0.7 VCCI, 0.3 VCCI.
*   The model switches its output at the middle of VIL and VIH; the tests then compare each input level with VIH and VIL themselves.
* output impedance (p6 Table 5.5): VOH at IOH = -12 mA, VCCO 3 V: 2.3 V, so (3.0-2.3)/12 mA = 58 ohm; VOL 0.7 V at 12 mA = 58 ohm; at 1.65 V: (1.65-1.2)/8 mA = 56 ohm, VOL 0.45 V at 8 mA = 56 ohm. Model uses 57 ohm (mean of the four ratios; MODEL CHOICE).
* control: OE high (p6 IOZ test, "OE = VIH") turns every port to high impedance; DIRn high = A to B (sch-notes.md 11.3 quoting function table, SCES898C); VCC isolation: below 0.1 V on either supply every port is Hi-Z (SCES898C, quoted in ecad/ring/sch-notes.md 11.3 line 3684 of the text copy).
.subckt SN74AXC4T774 a1 a2 a3 a4 b1 b2 b3 b4 vcca vccb dir1 dir2 dir3 dir4 oe
* usable = both supplies above 0.1 V and OE low (below 0.65 VCCA, control VIH)
Bus us 0 V = ( (v(vcca) > 0.1) && (v(vccb) > 0.1) && (v(oe) < 0.5*v(vcca)) ) ? 1 : 0
* thresholds for the A input (VCCA) and the B input (VCCB)
Bta ta 0 V = (v(vcca) >= 3.0) ? 1.4 : (v(vcca) >= 2.3) ? 1.15 : (v(vcca) >= 1.1) ? 0.5*(0.65+0.35)*v(vcca) : 0.5*(0.7+0.3)*v(vcca)
Btb tb 0 V = (v(vccb) >= 3.0) ? 1.4 : (v(vccb) >= 2.3) ? 1.15 : (v(vccb) >= 1.1) ? 0.5*(0.65+0.35)*v(vccb) : 0.5*(0.7+0.3)*v(vccb)
* channel n: dir high: A input drives B pin through 57 ohm to VCCB or 0; dir low: B input drives A pin through 57 ohm to VCCA or 0
.subckt CH a b vcca vccb dir us ta tb
Bab drvb 0 V = (v(a) > v(ta)) ? v(vccb) : 0
Bba drva 0 V = (v(b) > v(tb)) ? v(vcca) : 0
* current from the pin to its drive node through 57 ohm, only when the channel points that way and the part is usable
Gb b 0 value = ( (v(us) > 0.5) && (v(dir) > 0.5*v(vcca)) ) ? (v(b) - v(drvb))/57 : 0
Ga a 0 value = ( (v(us) > 0.5) && (v(dir) < 0.5*v(vcca)) ) ? (v(a) - v(drva))/57 : 0
* input leakage of the pin that is the input: 8 uA worst case at high level (SCES898C p6 Table 5.5 II data inputs, -40 to 125 C)
Blkb b 0 I = ( (v(us) > 0.5) && (v(dir) < 0.5*v(vcca)) ) ? 8u*min(max(v(b)/max(v(vccb),0.1),0),1) : 0
Blka a 0 I = ( (v(us) > 0.5) && (v(dir) > 0.5*v(vcca)) ) ? 8u*min(max(v(a)/max(v(vcca),0.1),0),1) : 0
* numerical only: 1e12 ohm from each port to ground so that an undriven port is not a floating node (1 pA at 1 V, far below every stated leakage)
Rfa a 0 1e12
Rfb b 0 1e12
.ends CH
X1 a1 b1 vcca vccb dir1 us ta tb CH
X2 a2 b2 vcca vccb dir2 us ta tb CH
X3 a3 b3 vcca vccb dir3 us ta tb CH
X4 a4 b4 vcca vccb dir4 us ta tb CH
.ends SN74AXC4T774
